WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.552
Every partner on Entra ID gets its own

2
00:00:02.552 --> 00:00:06.750
organization-specific entry in
cross-tenant access settings.

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.230
Those settings override the defaults,

4
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.725
and MFA and device claims from other
tenants aren't trusted by default.

5
00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:17.993
Inbound B2B collaboration is
allowed for the partner tenant only,

6
00:00:17.993 --> 00:00:20.813
scoped to the access
package's applications.

7
00:00:20.813 --> 00:00:23.174
B2B direct connect is blocked.

8
00:00:23.174 --> 00:00:28.288
Trusting the partner's MFA is turned on
only where the agreement says the partner

9
00:00:28.288 --> 00:00:32.867
enforces it at home, and Conditional
Access still requires the strength;

10
00:00:32.867 --> 00:00:35.538
trusting MFA only skips the second prompt.

11
00:00:35.538 --> 00:00:38.710
Trust in compliant or
hybrid-joined devices stays off,

12
00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:42.376
unless the agreement names the
partner's compliance standard.

13
00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:45.500
Automatic redemption stays
off on the default route.

14
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.284
The record holds the partner's immutable
tenant ID and the names it resolves to,

15
00:00:50.284 --> 00:00:54.700
and a partner domain that resolves to
another tenant is a stop condition.

16
00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:00.295
For a partner on SAML or WS-Fed federation,
Conditional Access can require only

17
00:01:00.295 --> 00:01:06.020
the MFA grant, so the agreement must say
whether the method is phishing-resistant.
